From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akram-composio <akram@composio.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:26:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] web: send signed-out visitors straight to Kimono sign-in
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Why: with Kimono, sign-in is Kimono's (an OIDC provider). Kimono sets
oauth.enabled + oauth.autoLaunch in the config file; people must never see the
Immich login form or a flash of it, and it must be testable with curl.

What must survive upstream changes:
- Server: the web index middleware (ApiService.ssr in server/src/services/
  api.service.ts, the catch-all that serves index.html) answers GET/HEAD `/` and
  `/auth/login` with a 302 to the OAuth authorize URL when OAuth is enabled with
  autoLaunch and the request has no valid session cookie. It sets the same
  immich_oauth_state / immich_oauth_code_verifier cookies as POST
  /api/oauth/authorize, with redirect_uri <origin>/auth/login (the URI the web
  app itself uses, so the existing callback page finishes the login). The
  origin is server.externalDomain when that names the request's host (so an
  untrusted proxy can't downgrade https), else the request's own origin.
  Logic lives in AuthService.getOAuthAutoLaunch / isAuthenticatedRequest.
- Escape hatches, never redirected: ?autoLaunch=0, ?password=1|true (upstream's
  own opt-outs, still showing the password form when password login is on), and
  OAuth callbacks (?code=… / ?error=…). Signed-in visitors get the app.
- If the provider can't be reached (discovery fails), the server logs a warning
  and serves the web app as usual.
- Web: the login page draws a flat cover instead of the form while it is
  auto-launching or completing a callback (deep links reach /auth/login
  client-side, not via the server); the form appears only on error or opt-out.
- Sign-out is upstream's: an OAuth session's logout returns the provider's
  end-session URL (oauth.endSessionEndpoint or discovery), so people land on
  Kimono's sign-out, not the Immich login page.
- No /api behaviour changes (the phone app depends on the API).

